    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40054" root="نظر" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَظِيرَةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَظُورٌ</span>, in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also, <i>A
scout,</i> or <i>scouts;</i> (T, Sgh, K;) and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَظُورَةٌ</span></b> :
(Sgh, K:) pl. of both, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَظَائِرُ</span>. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Fem.
of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَظِيرٌ</span>, q. v. (T, &amp;c.). [And hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">النَّظَائِرُ</span>
[the pl.] <i>The more excellent of men:</i> (K, * TA:)
because they resemble one another in dispositions
and actions and sayings. (TA.)

